+## D05 additive terminal proof scope (15 November 2026)
+
+Historical final proof `/1` and generic calibration-equivalence receipts retain
+their GenericRead-only meaning. New final proof `/2` may bind calibration `/2`
+with complete class dispositions and exact terminal qualification pins. Its
+`context_action_class_rules/2` task scope binds the final calibration identity.
+Each supported terminal class must have exactly one proof; unsupported classes
+may not acquire rules. A `/2` proof cannot reuse the generic-only calibration
+primitive-equivalence path to transfer terminal evidence. All existing numerical,
+resource, composed, held-out and rights gates still apply to the exact candidate.
+
+The recorded promotion decision separately approves terminal qualifications,
+human annotation sources, actual native raw captures, criteria freezes and
+repository-cluster independence analyses. The owner reads every exact file,
+reconciles input/roster/card/source/score identities, replays the unchanged raw
+global-winner rule on CAL and independent confirmation and recomputes acceptance
+counts, coverage and the zero-error one-sided95% bound. A supplied passing flag
+or effective sample count without its approved cluster analysis is insufficient.
+Human judgments are not generated by the native fitter or an agent. Missing
+labels/analysis means unsupported, not a reason to weaken limits or reuse generic
+Read certificates. Old `/1` serialized calibration fields remain absent.
+
+The exact pre-score criteria file also binds both native population identities
+and the complete semantic rule template with its margin zeroed. Confirmation
+uses the CAL-selected margin unchanged. Native closures bind actual score rows
+and their original receipt closure; approved metadata does not replace any
+existing exact-candidate final native/composed/held-out gate. The `/2` path
+retains Focus's relevance-only scope and the exact-three catalog requirement.
